# cuts/v1.0.24/cut.env -- the pins bin/rollforward_gate.sh binds for --cut v1.0.24
# ============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE LIVES IN CM051 AND NOT IN OS003
#
# cut.yml demands two things of a tag, and until 2026-08-13 they lived in
# different repos:
#
#   "Tag must match the in-repo cut record"  cut-manifests/<TAG>.yaml   CM051
#   "Rollforward claims" runs --cut <TAG>    cuts/<TAG>/cut.env         OS003
#
# Nothing carried the second across. scripts/sync_rollforward_registry.sh
# vendored four fixed paths and none was a cut.env, so `cuts/v*/cut.env` here
# matched NOTHING and --cut could not resolve for ANY tag. Not a missing
# v1.0.24; a missing category. The gate's own "Cuts with a cut.env:" hint
# printed an empty list under its error.
#
# Measured on the v1.0.24 tag push: PARSE ERROR, preflight red, cut job
# SKIPPED, nothing signed.
#
# THE FIX THAT WAS NOT THE FIX. The first attempt wrote the cut.env into OS003,
# which is not the repo the gate reads, and would have re-pushed the tag into
# the identical failure while looking, in OS003, exactly like a fix.
#
# THE SECOND ATTEMPT WAS ALSO WRONG, and is worth recording because it looked
# more principled. Vendoring OS003's cut.env files across via the sync script
# worked, and dragged 464 lines of operator working-record into the product
# repo with it: four private box IPs and five notarisation submission IDs.
# The gate reads exactly TWO keys --
#
#     OSTLER_PIN_OA="$(_cut_pin DAEMON_COMMIT)"
#     OSTLER_PIN_CM051="$(_cut_pin CM051)"
#
# -- and the mapping is DECLARED in the runner, not inferred. Everything else
# in those files is prose the gate never touches. So the file the gate reads
# belongs in the repo the gate runs in, holding only the declared keys, beside
# the cut-manifest it is paired with. OS003's cuts/v1.0.24/cut.env stays as the
# operator's fuller record; this is the machine-readable half.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon this DMG ships. gui/Makefile carries DAEMON_VERSION ?= 0.4.55 and
# fetches the published tarball, so the pin here must name the same build.
#
# RESOLVED AT SOURCE, AND THE FIRST ANSWER WAS THE WRONG OBJECT. hub-v0.4.55 is
# an ANNOTATED tag: the ref points at tag object d40c3535, and the commit is
# e0234e71. A pin recording d40c3535 would name an object that is not a commit,
# and every ancestry check against it would fail in a way that reads as a stale
# daemon rather than a malformed pin.
DAEMON_COMMIT=e0234e71c66d

# CM051 main at tag time -- 925919e1, the version bump (#604) that this cut
# exists to carry. Anything earlier declares 1.0.23 and fails the installer
# version-consistency step.
CM051=925919e1
